From f9c8de81f9055d40765d6632a00fed1a44ecff34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:15:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/57] hw/misc: Buzz Click (piezo buzzer on PWM); own CS per
 SPI Click socket

- click-buzzer: times the rising edges of its drive pin on the virtual
  clock; "frequency" (Hz) and "duty" (per mille) of the last period, 0
  once two periods pass without an edge; the first edge after a silence
  starts a new tone. Buzz Click schematic v100: PWM through R1 10k into
  Q1's base (modelled as a pull-down), jumper J2 (default).
- mikrobus: new Click "buzz"; up to four inputs and pulls per Click; an
  SPI Click's "cs" index is its socket number. Before, two SPI Clicks on
  one board (ext1=8x8g,ext2=7seg) stopped QEMU with "CS index '0x0' in
  use".
- pic32cm-mc00-cpro: ext1/ext2 help lists the shared catalog.
- qtests: Buzz Click on EXT1 and on mikroBUS 1 of the Nano Base; two SPI
  Clicks on one bus.

Not checked against a physical Buzz Click.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
